IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `il-interpretation-law`
IMPORT `il-interpretation-gate`
IMPORT `il-interpretation-definitions-law`

-- Tests for il-interpretation-definitions-law.l4 (the entries of Law s 3, except day, year and month, fiscal year).
-- Expected values were decided from the words of each entry before the module was run; a failing assertion is a
-- finding and none was edited to match the code. The facts in each fixture are the ones the entry names.

§ `Tests: the defined terms of s 3`

§§ `Fixtures: instruments`

`a law passed by the Knesset` MEANS `A candidate statute` WITH
    `passed by the Knesset as a law` IS TRUE
    `an ordinance given before the establishment of the State` IS FALSE
    `an ordinance of the Provisional Council of State` IS FALSE

`a mandate-era ordinance` MEANS `A candidate statute` WITH
    `passed by the Knesset as a law` IS FALSE
    `an ordinance given before the establishment of the State` IS TRUE
    `an ordinance of the Provisional Council of State` IS FALSE

`an ordinance of the Provisional Council` MEANS `A candidate statute` WITH
    `passed by the Knesset as a law` IS FALSE
    `an ordinance given before the establishment of the State` IS FALSE
    `an ordinance of the Provisional Council of State` IS TRUE

`something that is none of those` MEANS `A candidate statute` WITH
    `passed by the Knesset as a law` IS FALSE
    `an ordinance given before the establishment of the State` IS FALSE
    `an ordinance of the Provisional Council of State` IS FALSE

`a Knesset law as an instrument` MEANS Instrument WITH
    `taken as a statute` IS `a law passed by the Knesset`
    `the statute it was given by virtue of` IS NOTHING
    `of legislative effect` IS TRUE
    `given in writing` IS TRUE
    `a direction or appointment, or a notice, announcement, licence, permit or the like` IS FALSE
    `a direction` IS FALSE
    `an appointment` IS FALSE
    `a notice` IS FALSE
    `an announcement` IS FALSE
    `a licence` IS FALSE
    `a permit` IS FALSE
    `something like them` IS FALSE

`regulations made under a Knesset law` MEANS Instrument WITH
    `taken as a statute` IS `something that is none of those`
    `the statute it was given by virtue of` IS JUST `a law passed by the Knesset`
